                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A funny, janky mess that's entertaining for a few hours, and then you've seen pretty much everything. \n\nJohn the Zombie is an interesting concept, because you actually play as the zombie. The animations, ridiculous carnage, and overall absurdity are comical enough to make the game entertaining for a few hours. Seeing a zombie ride around the map on a horse is certainly something I didn't expect to see.\n\nUnfortunately, once the novelty wears off, there really isn't much reason to stay.\n\nThe controls are incredibly janky, the game is full of bugs, and there are plenty of visual glitches throughout the environments and layouts. The movements also feel rather clunky as well, like my character is dragging around cement blocks behind him. The animations aren't particularly interesting to look at once you've seen them a few times. The storyline is also complete rubbish, and a lot of the game feels more like you're watching a collection of goofy bugs and ridiculous situations than playing a properly polished experience. \n\nI don't recommend this for the $11.49 CAD they're asking for on the store page. If you have a dollar or two to spare and just want something stupid to boot up and laugh at for a few hours when and if it goes on sale, it's not bad.\n\nJust keep in mind that you're not buying some masterpiece of a game. You're buying a game you boot up, laugh at for a few hours, and probably never turn on again.\n\nFor that kind of experience, a couple of bucks? Sure, why not.\n\nAt $11.49 CAD? \n\nHELL NAW.",
